<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug builds only (this file is in src/debug, so release builds keep Android's https-only default).

  The local test stack (apps/test-server, docs/TESTING.md) serves the homeserver over plain http and its
  LiveKit/lk-jwt call servers advertise http:// media and websocket URLs. The Matrix client (the Rust core)
  talks http regardless, but the call path is a Java HTTP client and Android refuses cleartext for it, so
  joining a voice room on the test stack failed with "CLEARTEXT communication ... not permitted".

  Cleartext is allowed for every host because the test stack's address is not fixed (127.0.0.1 through an
  adb forward, 10.0.2.2 on the emulator, the VM's LAN address on a USB phone). Nothing here ships: a
  release build has no networkSecurityConfig from this file (the one it gets is the Rust TLS verifier's,
  which forbids cleartext), so release keeps the platform default of no cleartext.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
